my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
line one
line two
line three
END_CODE

{
    desc => q{u undoes a line delete (dd)},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/undo_line_delete`

Tests that **u** restores a line deleted by **dd**.
This is a round-trip test: start and end states look the same.

**Keys:** `dd`, `u`

**initial.png**
- Buffer has 3 lines: "line one", "line two", "line three"
- Cursor on line 1

**after_dd.png**
- Buffer has 2 lines: "line two", "line three"
- Line 1 ("line one") was deleted
- Cursor on the new line 1
- Intermediate snapshot showing the changed state

**after_undo.png**
- Buffer restored to 3 lines (identical to initial)
- Cursor back on line 1
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('dd');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_dd');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('u');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_undo');
    },
}
